@format 1
@id functionality.media-loading.common.list-add
@title Media loading — common Files intake
@section Functionality
@area Media loading — Common
@entry paths-submitted
@summary Trace accepted paths through media discovery, docket insertion, and first-new-item selection.
@related functionality.media-loading.split, functionality.media-loading.edit, functionality.media-loading.convert, functionality.media-loading.audio, functionality.media-loading.merge, functionality.media-loading.funnel
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag common
@tag files

@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket

[paths-submitted] Paths submitted to Files <input>
= An accepted picker, drop, relay, delivery, or Merge-group request has supplied file-system paths to the shared Files intake.
> media-scan

[media-scan] Media path discovery <process>
- Keep supported existing media files supplied directly, recursively enumerate supplied folders, and skip inaccessible folders after logging the failure @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
> scan-result

[scan-result] Scan result <decision>
- Continue to docket insertion only when discovery produced supported media paths @ list.PListPathsAdd(...)
? "Supported media discovered" > docket-add
? "No supported media" > scan-empty

[scan-empty] Nothing discovered <output>
= No docket entry is added and no selected-path publication occurs.

[docket-add] Docket insertion <process>
- Ignore paths already present, create a batch when necessary, add new entries, and publish docket change and added-entry notifications @ docket.LDocketPathsAdd(...)
> add-result

[add-result] Docket-add result <decision>
- Select the first newly added entry when the Files panel receives the added-entry notification @ list.PListDocketAddHandle(...)
? "At least one new entry" > current-publish
? "All discovered paths already listed" > add-empty

[add-empty] No new docket entry <output>
= Existing entries are left in place and no first-new-item selection is published.

[current-publish] First new path publication <process>
- Set the first newly added path as current and publish the Files path-change event @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
> selected-path-output

[selected-path-output] Current Files path published <output>
= The active tab's scenario-specific selected-path adapter receives the new current path.
